description: Require explicit Program classes and startup methods for entry points.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Entry Points

- Never use top-level statements for APIs, Function Apps, console apps, workers, or any executable entry point.
- Always use an explicit `Program` class with a `Main` method.
- Follow `.cursor/rules/host-composition.mdc` for host bootstrap details.
- Do not delegate `Main` to a separate application startup class.

```csharp
// BAD - top-level statements
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder( args );
var app = builder.Build();
app.Run();

// BAD - Main delegates everything away
public static void Main( string[] args )
    => HostApplication.Run( args );

// GOOD - see host-composition.mdc for the full pattern
public class Program
{
    private static void Main( string[] args )
    {
        // try/catch, ConfigureDefaultHostApplication, ConfigurePipeline, app.Run()
    }
}
```
